le who  qualify to serve some of the pentagon's  own data suggest that more than 70  percent of 17 to 24 year olds young  people in this country do not reach do  not meet the educational psychological  uh or or physical requirements that's a  national security issue is it not it is  the air force is meeting its recruiting  goals for active force we're a little  bit short this year on the garden  reserve  and we're doing a number of things to  address that  basically the opportunity to serve in  the military particularly for me the air  force or the space force is a tremendous  opportunity and we just need to  communicate that to people you get a  chance to do interesting exciting and  important work you get to serve your  country uh you get to prepare yourself  for a career either in the service or  outside of it uh in a very positive way  so we're we're actively upping our  recruiting game i was going to ask you  what's your pitch and you've just sort  of laid out the pitch very nice i wasn't  going to miss the opportunity i i find  it very very compelling i almost went to  a service academy out of uh high school  uh and but i it does concern me looking  at the number of young people who don't  even if they want to serve they can't i  mean how do you change that  we're making some modifications for  where people are going to have jobs that  aren't as physically demanding as some  military jobs space force for example is  making some changes there uh some jobs  in the air force some jobs require a lot  of physical capability  almost all of our jobs require  reasonable mental capability uh  intellectual capability  so we're doing some things to adjust on  our side as well you also mentioned  space force can you just what exactly is  it who gets to join who gets to play and  how does that work what are your goals  there because we all hear the term space  force it means many things to different  people the space force is now coming up  on three years old uh it was created  primarily out of air force units but  also units from the navy  and the army as well uh it's a  relatively small service it's similar in  some ways to the marine corps being part  of the department of the navy and that  the space force is part of the  department of the air force how many  people in space force would you say  active duty it's about 8 500  so it's it's relatively small but it's  very important the mission is critical  to our national security  uh the programs that they do and the  services that they provide as well as  the ability to contest for control of  space which is becoming increasingly  necessary is a really important mission  mr secretary i've got a genuine question  about ufos not as like little green men  and aliens but the idea that there could  be some sort of technique  yeah you got the secretary to laugh and  smile for a moment there so i think  that's that's a good question no i mean  the ufc what's wrong with little greek  man i mean there's military video uh of  aviators who have seen things that  cannot be explained right and there's an  active investigation i think the worry  is not that it's little green men but  that it's a a another country with  technology that we've not seen before so  what where from where you sit are ufos a  real issue  um to be quite honest not for me um i  have real threats that i worry about  every day and there's severe threats  um i'm aware of i don't have direct  responsibility for investigating uh  these phenomena uh i've looked at the  reports i've seen what's been there  there are things that we haven't been  able to explain but i think that the  important thing for us to do is do some  ex some real technical investigation of  what they are and try to resolve these  i'm curious about what you really do  worry about you said it's not a worry  for you what do you really worry about  as you sit here today with us china  china china  i came back into government  after being out for 15 years in 2010  and i observed right away that china was  from the intelligence reports that china  was trying to fuel the set of  capabilities designed to defeat the  united states in the vicinity of china  to deny its ability to project power  close to the vicinity of china and in  the last dozen years they've continued  down that path they've been fairly  open-minded and innovative  technically reasonably sophisticated  they've identified what they think are  the the high value targets for them to  attack  includes things like aircraft carriers  our forward air bases and our satellites  in space  uh and so we have a formidable problem  there that we have to address and so  when people say that why are you  spending money on the next generation of  fighters f-22s and f-35s when we have  aircraft already capable of destroying  95 of the world's air forces you say  because we're not focused on those  threats this is the threat the pacing  challenge as we call it is china and  it's because of their military  modernization program they have the the  resources they have the strategic intent  and they have the capability and the  scale to basically contest the united  states as dominance  we've been very comfortable with our  position of dominance since the first  gulf war too comfortable frankly i'm i'm  a i'm i was a cold warrior i spent the  first 20 years of my career worrying  about the soviet union so i know  viscerally what it is like to have a  pure competitor we have one and if i  were to characterize china today i'd say  it is more severe of a competitor than  the soviet union was in 1983 you're  saying  your 75th anniversary you're still new  to the job you like it i love the job  i've got a great leadership team i've  got a very important mission that  everybody's dedicated to and performing  very well at it's a very professional  organization i'm delighted to have the  opportunity to secretary kendall  congratulations on 75 years uh the air  force not you personally but